  "findings": {
    "decision": "Retain the optional Int64 cast/add fusion; investigate the remaining complete-query cost and shared-path overhead separately.",
    "complete_query": "DOUBLE with final Decimal output improves 4.094%, with a paired 95% interval of -4.227% to -3.957%. Its instruction count falls 1.547%. This improvement exceeds recorded same-binary control shifts.",
    "native_queries": "Derived DOUBLE native output improves 75.645% and stored FLOAT/integer native output improves 24.731%. Instructions fall 15.841% and 21.760%.",
    "remaining_precision_gap": "The full DOUBLE/FLOAT Decimal time difference is 18.946% before and 13.898% after in this fixed experiment. It is not eliminated. These expressions have different general arithmetic semantics.",
    "shared_path": "Shared DOUBLE addition records +1.572% elapsed time (paired 95% interval +0.583% to +3.242%) and +0.420% instructions. Same-binary shifts are -0.098% before and -0.689% after. This dispatch cost remains to be reduced; no zero-overhead claim.",
    "change": "An existing RHS CastExpr to Float64 is evaluated once through its original child. An Int64 child can be converted in the owned-left addition loop with the same as-f64 operation used by num_traits. Other source types retain the original cast options. Unavailable left ownership or scalar inputs retain separate casting and native borrowed addition.",
    "correctness": "81 native binary tests, including 320 physical-expression comparisons against separate casts across length, NULLs, safe mode, ownership, scalar/array source types and overflow mode. Big integer rounding boundaries, i64 limits, non-finite floats and invalid strings are covered. 37 planner and 28 runner tests including four Delta lifecycle tests pass. All 258 benchmark checks/plans, 6784 SQL observation classifications and successful values/types, and 116 Delta parent comparisons remain unchanged.",
    "scope": "Native DataFusion BinaryExpr only, with no new node or dependency. Both rejected allocation prototypes are excluded. Default vendor sources remain unchanged.",
    "coverage_limit": "Performance inputs are finite and non-NULL at batch size 8192. Existing Spark differences and the remaining full-query cost persist.",
    "next_step": "Specialize the fused and normal addition helpers at compile time and avoid inspecting RHS cast nodes when the left array is shared, then measure the same controls before retaining that refinement."
  },
